# Proposal 1 — zcode-parity-doctrine.md paths: frontmatter

> **Apply to:** `.claude/rules/zcode-parity-doctrine.md`
> **Origin:** session-start-token-audit S2 §1 table row 1 + Note A (binding).
> **Mechanism:** CC-native conditional load. A rule with `paths:` frontmatter is loaded by
> Claude Code only when the session reads files matching the listed globs (CC docs: "Path-scoped
> rules trigger when Claude reads files matching the pattern"). The `<!-- globs: -->` marker
> this rule already carries (currently at line 8) does NOT restrict the CC-native loader —
> only `paths:` does. Pasting the marker's comma-separated string as a scalar yields either
> "rule never loads" or "rule stays always-on" — both silently. Each glob must be a YAML list
> item.
> **Token impact:** 22,177 bytes / ~5,544 tokens removed from every session-start (host-cc +
> aif-container). Source: S1 attribution table row for `zcode-parity-doctrine.md`.
> **Diff verification:** mechanically generated + `git apply --check` returns clean against the
> pre-application HEAD of `feature/session-start-token-audit-c781e8` (commit 336d031ef, 2026-07-30).

## The diff (apply with `git apply`)

```diff
diff --git a/.claude/rules/zcode-parity-doctrine.md b/.claude/rules/zcode-parity-doctrine.md
--- a/.claude/rules/zcode-parity-doctrine.md
+++ b/.claude/rules/zcode-parity-doctrine.md
@@ -1,3 +1,12 @@
+---
+paths:
+  - .claude/hooks/**
+  - scripts/render-harness-config.mjs
+  - plugin/hooks/**
+  - docs/meta-factory/zcode-parity-mega.*.md
+  - docs/meta-factory/research-patches/2026-07-18-zcode-parity-*.md
+---
+
 # ZCode parity doctrine — discipline rule

 > **Class:** A — companion principle test shipped at [packages/core/principles/09-doc-authority-hierarchy.test.ts](../../packages/core/principles/09-doc-authority-hierarchy.test.ts) (doctrine registered in `REQUIRED_HEADER_DOCS`; the doctrine itself is a SSOT pointer-aggregator, the enforcement lives in existing gates per §6).
```

(The diff's @@ -1,3 +1,12 @@ hunk header reflects: 3 -side context lines (`# title`, blank, `> Class:`) → 12 +side lines (9 added + 3 context). The hunk is minimal — it only adds the frontmatter block + trailing blank.)

## Apply recipe

```bash
# 1. Apply the diff (maintainer hands; agents are deny-listed on .claude/**):
git apply docs/meta-factory/research-patches/2026-07-26-session-start-token-audit-proposals/01-zcode-parity-doctrine-paths-frontmatter.diff
# Verify it applied:
head -12 .claude/rules/zcode-parity-doctrine.md

# 2. Verify NO line-number citations need shifting (mechanically verified at proposal
#    authoring time 2026-07-30):
git grep -nE 'zcode-parity-doctrine\.md:[0-9]+' -- ':!docs/meta-factory/research-patches/2026-07-26-session-start-token-audit-proposals/'
# Expected: EMPTY. At S2 authoring time, NO file in the repo cites this rule by :line-number
# (no rule, doc, test, or kickoff references `zcode-parity-doctrine.md:<N>`). The line-shift
# caused by the 9-line frontmatter insertion is therefore a non-event — but step is retained
# as a binding re-verification, not a busywork step. If the grep returns hits, update each
# cited line number to its new (shifted-by-+9) value.

# 3. Verify CC-native loader honours the new frontmatter (live session start):
#    Start a fresh CC session in this repo, edit a file under .claude/hooks/, and confirm
#    the rule appears in the loaded context. Then start a session editing an unrelated file
#    (e.g. README.md) and confirm the rule is ABSENT.

# 4. Verify dual-pair invariant: the existing <!-- globs: --> marker (post-shift line ~17)
#    must carry the SAME glob set as paths: above. Compare comma-split to the paths: list —
#    they must be set-equal (per rule-enforcement-channel-selection.md §4 "Keep the two glob
#    sets identical"):
grep -A1 '<!-- globs:' .claude/rules/zcode-parity-doctrine.md
```

## Why this is safe

- 15 rules already use `paths:` frontmatter (verified at S1; e.g. `ci-tool-pinning.md:3-9`).
- zcode-parity-doctrine is already registered in principle 09 `REQUIRED_HEADER_DOCS`
  (`packages/core/principles/09-doc-authority-hierarchy.ts:28-55`) — frontmatter and the
  doc-authority header coexist fine (15 precedents).
- The rule's `Fires:` clause (currently line 4) already enumerates exactly these paths — the
  rule was DESIGNED to fire only on this scope, but the CC-native loader ignored that intent
  and loaded it always. This proposal aligns the runtime behaviour with the declared intent.

## Risks if misapplied

- **Pasting as scalar** (`paths: .claude/hooks/**, scripts/render-harness-config.mjs, ...`)
  produces silent no-op (rule stays always-on) — the YAML parses as a single string, not a
  list. Each glob MUST be a `- ` list item. The diff above uses the correct list form.
- **Forgetting the `---` terminator** makes the frontmatter body part of the rule body —
  silent parse failure. The diff includes both opening and closing `---`.
- **Missing the re-grep step (step 2)** would leave stale `:N` citations if any exist — at
  proposal authoring time none do, but new citations added between S2 and the maintainer's
  application could exist; re-verify.
